{
  "summary": "This study investigates kinetic-environmental coupling at buried interfaces in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells. Using dual-side in situ photoluminescence, it reveals simultaneous nucleation at gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during processing. Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, causing kinetic mismatch that worsens moisture damage. The researchers designed a self-segregating molecule (NFA) that enriches at the buried interface to synchronize crystallization, passivate defects, and form a hydrophobic barrier. This approach achieved record power conversion efficiencies of 24.84% in small cells and 21.46% in mini-modules, maintaining 96.26% efficiency after 1000h damp aging at 85±5% RH.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Simultaneous nucleation occurs at both gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing",
    "Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, exacerbating moisture damage",
    "Self-segregating molecule NFA synchronizes crystallization, passivates defects, and forms a hydrophobic barrier"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes self-segregated interfacial regulation as a rational strategy to overcome kinetic-environmental constraints in scalable flexible perovskite photovoltaics."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how early human settlement in the Arabian desert was influenced by stone availability for tool production, beyond water resources. Using a 1,500-km geoarchaeological survey across Rub' al Khali, researchers found no lithic artefacts or knappable materials where freshwater existed but stone was scarce. Spatial analysis indicates settlement required co-occurrence of water and lithic resources, with 57% of water-accessible terrain lacking suitable stone. This challenges models that prioritize water alone for predicting human dispersal.",
  "key_findings": [
    "No lithic artefacts or knappable raw materials were found in 55 of 125 surveyed localities despite abundant freshwater",
    "Spatial modeling shows 57% of water-accessible terrain lacks knappable stone, reducing false positives in site identification",
    "Convergent patterns across Africa, North America, and Asia suggest stone availability is a universal constraint on early human dispersal"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings demonstrate that lithic resource availability, not water alone, critically constrained early human dispersal across arid regions, refining models of Pleistocene human migration."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated how protein kinase A (PKA) signaling regulates group 3 innate lymphoid cell (ILC3) homeostasis and its role in gut inflammation. Using a single-cell atlas, researchers found that prostaglandin activates PKA to promote tissue-protective functions, while interleukin-23 (IL-23) suppresses PKA inhibitors. Deletion of PRKAR1A reduced ILC3s and increased infection susceptibility in mice, and human ILC3s expressed PRKAR1A, which was downregulated by IL-23 in inflammation. These findings indicate PKA signaling is critical for maintaining ILC3s and that IL-23-driven PKA dysregulation causes gut inflammation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "IL-23 suppresses PKA inhibitors in ILC3s, promoting inflammation",
    "PRKAR1A deletion reduced ILC3s and increased enteric infection susceptibility in mice",
    "Human intestinal ILC3s express PRKAR1A, downregulated by IL-23 in inflammatory bowel disease"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes PKA signaling as a key regulator of ILC3 homeostasis and demonstrates how IL-23 disrupts this balance to drive gut inflammation, providing mechanistic insights into inflammatory bowel disease pathogenesis."
}

{
  "summary": "This study examines how undisturbed soil practices influence agricultural resilience and risk in African contexts. By analyzing conservation agriculture's impact on soil health and farming systems, it identifies reduced erosion and improved water retention as key outcomes. These findings suggest that maintaining soil structure without disturbance enhances long-term sustainability in African farming communities.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Reduced soil erosion through undisturbed soil practices",
    "Improved water retention capacity in agricultural systems",
    "Enhanced resilience to climate variability in African farming contexts"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The research demonstrates that preserving soil structure without disturbance strengthens agricultural resilience in African contexts, contributing to sustainable land management practices under climate change pressures."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates shear alignment polymer extrusion (SHAPE) 3D printing for fabricating high-loading nanocomposites with long-range ordered nanostructures. The approach uses high shear forces to align nanofillers like boron nitride nanosheets and carbon nanotubes in polymer matrices, enabling complex 3D architectures at scalable loadings (up to 55 wt%). Results show zero volume shrinkage, exceptional thermomechanical stability, and tailored thermal conductivity (1.07 W/m/K) or insulation (0.071 W/m/K) depending on alignment direction.",
  "key_findings": [
    "SHAPE 3D printing achieves high nanofiller loadings (55 wt% boron nitride) without compromising structural integrity",
    "Aligned nanocomposites exhibit tailored thermal properties: vertically aligned structures show high thermal conductivity (1.07 W/m/K), horizontally aligned ones provide thermal insulation (0.071 W/m/K)",
    "Post-sintered materials maintain zero volume shrinkage and thermomechanical stability up to polymer decomposition temperatures"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This method enables scalable fabrication of nanocomposites with precisely engineered nanostructures for thermal management and structural applications, bridging nanoscale functionality and macroscale geometry."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether brief dietary changes during acute inflammation influence long-term tissue immune memory. Using lean mice with early type 17 skin inflammation, researchers found that a 4-day high-fat diet (HFD) exposure at disease onset exacerbates inflammation comparably to chronic obesity. The effect is confined to a specific 4-day window; HFD outside this window has no impact. Switching obese mice to low-fat diet during the same window prevents disease amplification. Mechanistically, HFD rapidly recruits neutrophils, which express Nlrp3 and Il1b, activating a neutrophil-NLRP3-IL-1β axis that licenses pathogenic TH17 cells. After recovery, chromatin-poised tissue-resident memory T cells persist, causing exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence despite subsequent low-fat diet. Transient HFD also amplifies lung TH17 inflammation via similar mechanisms. These findings demonstrate that dietary state during a narrow temporal window can durably reprogram disease trajectory by embedding short-lived physiological states in local immune memory.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Transient high-fat diet exposure at disease onset exacerbates acute type 17 skin inflammation in lean mice to levels comparable with chronic obesity.",
    "The pro-inflammatory effect is restricted to a 4-day peri-initiation window; HFD outside this window has no impact.",
    "Neutrophil recruitment and NLRP3-IL-1β signaling drive pathogenic TH17 cell activation, with persistent tissue-resident memory T cells causing exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence despite dietary recovery."
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes that dietary state during a narrow temporal window can durably reprogram immune memory, revealing a mechanism by which transient physiological states embed in tissue inflammation to influence long-term disease trajectories."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated methods to balance privacy protection with statistical accuracy in census data. Using a novel algorithm, it demonstrated that enhanced privacy measures can maintain or improve the precision of population statistics without compromising data utility. The findings suggest that privacy-preserving techniques may not inherently reduce statistical reliability.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A new algorithm enables privacy protection while maintaining census data accuracy",
    "Enhanced privacy measures do not diminish statistical precision in population statistics",
    "The approach supports reliable population statistics without compromising data utility"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes that privacy-preserving techniques can coexist with high accuracy in census data, advancing the theoretical framework for secure statistical reporting."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the long-standing challenge of achieving stable photocatalytic pure water splitting over Ta3N5 by identifying incompatibility between cocatalysts in alkaline systems and pure water splitting as the critical bottleneck. The researchers developed a highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst using a multi-step incipient wetness impregnation strategy. The optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx photocatalyst achieved stoichiometric water splitting with an apparent quantum yield of 0.72% at 420 nm, the highest reported for Ta-based nitrides/oxynitrides. Mechanistic insights indicate enhanced interfacial electric fields and reduced reaction barriers improve hole extraction and intermediate kinetics.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Identification of cocatalyst incompatibility between alkaline water oxidation and pure water splitting as the critical bottleneck for Ta3N5 photocatalysts",
    "Development of a highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst via multi-step incipient wetness impregnation",
    "Optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx achieved 0.72% apparent quantum yield for stoichiometric water splitting at 420 nm"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes cocatalyst compatibility as a fundamental design principle for stable photocatalytic water splitting over nitride-based materials, providing mechanistic insights for advancing solar-driven water splitting technologies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the demographic origins of Celtic languages using ancient genomic data from 4,587 Bronze and Iron Age European individuals. By analyzing genome-wide data, the researchers identified three key population movements: Steppe-related ancestry arriving via Bell Beaker groups around 4400 BP, a Bronze Age migration from southwestern Europe to Britain, and a westward expansion of eastern central European ancestry (3200-2800 BP) affecting France, the British Isles, Iberia, and Italy. The findings suggest that the eastern central European migration is the most parsimonious explanation for Celtic language spread, though language shifts may not directly follow genetic patterns.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Steppe-related ancestry entered Europe via Bell Beaker groups approximately 4400 years ago",
    "Bronze Age migration from southwestern Europe to Britain occurred between 3800-3200 BP",
    "Eastern central European ancestry expanded westward from 3200-2800 BP, influencing regions where Celtic languages later emerged"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides genomic evidence supporting a specific demographic pathway for Celtic language dispersal in prehistoric Europe, resolving debates about the origins and spread of Celtic languages through ancient population movements."
}

{
  "summary": "This study employed computational modeling to simulate child language acquisition, focusing on how individual children develop linguistic skills. The model successfully replicated critical milestones in early language development, including vocabulary growth and grammatical complexity. The findings suggest that individual variation in language learning processes can be captured through computational approaches, offering insights into the mechanisms underlying early communication skills.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Computational models accurately reproduced key features of child language development",
    "The approach captured individual differences in vocabulary acquisition and grammatical complexity",
    "The study demonstrated that computational methods can model individual child language learning trajectories"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The research provides a computational framework for understanding individual variability in early language acquisition, advancing models of how children develop linguistic abilities through structured learning processes."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing perovskite solar cell efficiency and stability using covalent organic frameworks (COFs). Researchers developed an in situ polymerization strategy to form COF networks at grain boundaries during annealing, avoiding pre-synthesized COF agglomeration. The approach improved crystallization, defect passivation, and hydrophobicity, achieving a 26.74% power conversion efficiency and enhanced stability.",
  "key_findings": [
    "In situ polymerization of COFs at grain boundaries during annealing prevents COF agglomeration",
    "The strategy enhances crystallization quality, defect passivation, and hydrophobicity",
    "SAS-treated perovskite solar cells achieved 26.74% power conversion efficiency and improved stability"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a novel method for integrating COF networks into perovskite solar cells to simultaneously achieve high efficiency and stability through controlled in situ assembly."
}

{
  "summary": "This study developed AutoDNA, an AI-native autonomous laboratory for biomolecular operations. The system integrates AI with multi-instrument workflows to execute nucleic acid synthesis, transcription, amplification, and sequencing with minimal human intervention. It achieved expert-level DNA synthesis yields, accelerated protocol execution 3.2-fold, completed DNA data storage cycles with exact content recovery, and identified a clinically relevant KRAS mutation through autonomous experimentation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "AutoDNA autonomously executes core nucleic acid operations across 20+ instrument types",
    "It matched expert-optimized DNA synthesis yields and accelerated protocol execution 3.2-fold",
    "Completed end-to-end DNA data storage cycles with exact digital content recovery"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes an AI-native framework for autonomous biomolecular experimentation, advancing the capability for multi-objective, end-to-end scientific workflows with minimal human oversight."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates fault recovery mechanisms following large earthquakes using long-term monitoring data. The research tracks how faults relock for subsequent seismic events after a major rupture. Key findings indicate that fault relocking occurs over extended periods, with implications for understanding earthquake recurrence intervals and seismic hazard assessment.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Fault relocking occurs over extended periods post-earthquake",
    "Monitoring reveals fault relocking precedes future seismic events",
    "Findings inform earthquake recurrence interval models"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides critical insights into fault behavior dynamics, enhancing understanding of how seismic systems prepare for future earthquakes through long-term relocking processes."
}

{
  "summary": "This study engineered dendritic cells (DCs) trained with inactivated bacteria and armored with MnO2 nanoparticles (MnArmL-trDCs) to enhance tumor infiltration and immune activation. The MnO2 layer masks immunological ligands in circulation, rendering DCs biologically silent and resistant to clearance. Upon reaching tumors, the DCs undergo pH- and H2O2-triggered transformation, promoting TLR/NLR/cGAS-STING pathway activation, cytotoxic lymphocyte infiltration, and synergy with anti-PD-1 therapy for sustained tumor regression.",
  "key_findings": [
    "MnO2-armed DCs mask immunological ligands in circulation, reducing immune recognition and hepatic clearance",
    "Tumor microenvironment triggers DC transformation via pH and hydrogen peroxide, enhancing tumor penetration",
    "M's strategy synergizes with anti-PD-1 therapy to achieve sustained tumor regression"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This nano-engineered cell armor strategy provides a generalizable platform for enhancing immune cell functionality in cancer immunotherapy by enabling precise phenotypic control and mechano-responsive activation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how animals integrate oral flavour signals with post-ingestive nutrient cues to learn about food's nutritional content. Using mice and humans, researchers identified a dopamine pathway in the anterior basolateral amygdala that selectively responds to post-ingestive nutrients. This pathway is critical for flavour-nutrient learning, as disrupting it impairs the association between taste and nutrient content, revealing a neural mechanism for nutritional learning.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Dopamine neurons in the ventral tegmental area are necessary for associating nutrients with flavours",
    "Post-ingestive nutrients trigger dopamine release selectively in the anterior basolateral amygdala",
    "Silencing anterior basolateral amygdala neurons prevents flavour-nutrient learning"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study establishes a specific neural circuit that integrates gustatory and post-ingestive signals to drive nutrient learning, advancing understanding of how animals assess food quality."
}

{
  "summary": "This review evaluates evidence on obesity pharmacotherapies' impact on cognition, focusing on GLP-1-based treatments and related pathways. It examines how cardiometabolic health improvements, direct neural effects, and disease stage influence cognitive outcomes. Findings indicate mixed results across studies, highlighting the complexity of cognitive effects in obesity treatments.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Mixed evidence from preclinical, observational, and clinical studies on cognitive effects of obesity pharmacotherapies",
    "GLP- 1-based therapies and related pathways are central to understanding cognitive outcomes in obesity treatments",
    "Cognitive effects may stem from direct neural actions or improved cardiometabolic health, depending on disease stage and metabolic context"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review clarifies the mechanisms underlying cognitive effects of obesity pharmacotherapies, distinguishing between direct neural actions and indirect cardiometabolic benefits to inform targeted interventions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study developed a 3D cuprous iodide cluster covalent organic framework (CuI-MCOF) with diamond topology for ultrasensitive HF detection. The sensor exhibits a 7188% response to 100 ppm HF at room temperature, with 3-second response and 2-second recovery times at 4 ppm. It achieves a detection limit of 21 ppb and maintains selectivity against 16 interfering gases at 100 ppm each, enabling real-time monitoring applications.",
  "key_findings": [
    "CuI-MCOF demonstrates a 7188% response to 100 ppm HF at room temperature",
    "The sensor achieves a 21 ppb detection limit and 3s/2s response/recovery times at 4 ppm",
    "It maintains stable HF detection in the presence of 16 interfering gases at 100 ppm each"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work advances HF sensing technology by establishing a cluster-based covalent organic framework with exceptional sensitivity, selectivity, and real-time performance for trace hydrogen fluoride detection."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether atom probe tomography (APT) can distinguish interstitial hydrogen in solution from defect-trapped hydrogen in metals. Using deuterium in FCC multi-principal-element alloys with coherent precipitates, the researchers demonstrated reproducible deuterium concentration in hydrogen-affinitive phases, aligning with theoretical predictions. The findings confirm APT's capability to analyze hydrogen in solid solution, advancing understanding of hydrogen partitioning in structural alloys for hydrogen-related applications.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Deuterium atoms reproducibly concentrate in hydrogen-affinitive phases within FCC multi-principal-element alloys",
    "Deuterium content differences correlate with distinct local chemistries and crystal structures",
    "Results align with theoretical predictions of hydrogen solution energies"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes atom probe tomography as a viable method for characterizing interstitial hydrogen in solid solution, providing critical insights into hydrogen partitioning mechanisms in structural alloys relevant to hydrogen storage and energy technologies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the relocking process of the megathrust following the 2011 Tohoku earthquake using 14 years of seafloor geodetic data, onshore observations, repeating earthquake analyses, and numerical modeling. It reveals that locking recovery was interrupted by afterslip and stress relaxation in the upper mantle, yet the megath. has reached a pre-earthquake locking state despite ongoing processes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The megathrust relocking process was interrupted by afterslip on the megathrust",
    "Stress relaxation occurred in the viscoelastic upper mantle during recovery",
    "The megathrust has achieved a locking state comparable to pre-earthquake conditions despite ongoing stress relaxation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings provide critical insights into the postseismic behavior of subduction zones, clarifying how megathrust locking states recover after great earthquakes through a combination of seismic and viscoelastic processes."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing fullerene C60's theoretical capacity in alkali-ion batteries by engineering two-dimensional covalent networks. The researchers synthesized tetragonal (TP-2D-C60) and hexagonal (HP-2D-C60) C60 nanosheets, achieving 522.0 mAh g-1 in lithium-ion batteries—exceeding pristine C60's 3.4 mAh g-1. DFT calculations indicate higher lithium binding sites and lower migration barriers in TP-2D-C60. The material also functions effectively in sodium-ion batteries.",
  "key_findings": [
    "TP-2D-C60 achieves 522.0 mAh g-1 in lithium-ion batteries, surpassing pristine C60's 3.4 mAh g-1",
    "DFT calculations reveal TP-2D-C60 has higher lithium binding sites and lower migration barriers than HP-2D-C60",
    "TP-2D-C60 demonstrates high capacity in sodium-ion batteries (309.9 mAh g-1)"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a strategy to overcome fullerene's theoretical capacity limits in alkali-ion batteries through structural engineering, enabling higher capacities than the molecular limit."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how the twist angle in twisted bilayer MoTe2 influences quantum phase transitions. Using transport measurements across 3.79°-5.76° twist angles, researchers observed an evolution from valley-polarized fractional topological states to valley-degenerate correlated states and superconductivity. The phase diagram reveals transitions between fractional quantum anomalous Hall states, integer quantum anomalous Hall insulators, and superconductivity as twist angle increases.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Evolution from valley-polarized fractional topological states to valley-degenerate correlated states and superconductivity across 3.79°-5.76° twist angles",
    "At small twist angles, partially filled Chern bands host fractional quantum anomalous Hall states following the Jain sequence",
    "Superconductivity emerges near νh = 1 at twist angles above ~5.6°, resembling twisted bilayer WSe2 phase diagrams"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a unified mechanism for twist-angle-driven quantum phase evolution in moiré systems, linking fractional topology, symmetry breaking, and superconductivity through systematic phase diagram mapping."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates ultracold quantum gases in microgravity using optical dipole traps. Researchers created a Bose-Einstein condensate aboard the China Space Station with 20,000 atoms at an equivalent temperature of 10 pK, achieving a free expansion time of 7 seconds. The record-low temperature enables advanced quantum simulations and precision measurements in space environments.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Bose-Einstein condensate achieved at 10 picokelvin equivalent temperature",
    "Free expansion time of 7.0 seconds in microgravity",
    "20,00:00 atoms in optical dipole trap system"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a new benchmark for ultracold quantum gas temperatures in space, advancing capabilities for quantum simulation and precision measurements under microgravity conditions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study developed a magnetically-gated haptic locomotion display (MHLD) using a flexible AC-driven quantum-dot LED coupled with a magnetoresponsive elastom. External magnetic fields induce actuator deformation, modulating contact with the display to trigger motion-coupled electroluminescence. Emission area and intensity scale with mechanical displacement, achieving 396 cd m-2 luminance. The system enables programmable directional motion and stable operation for haptic feedback applications.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Magnetic fields induce actuator deformation that modulates contact with the quantum-dot LED",
    "Emission area and intensity directly correlate with mechanical displacement magnitude",
    "The device achieves 396 cd m-2 luminance with programmable directional motion"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a novel mechanism for motion-coupled light emission in haptic displays, enabling direct mechanical displacement-to-light emission coupling without external electronics."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how ecological and social factors influence courtship behavior in Drosophila erecta. Using group aggregation on food patches, researchers demonstrated that food volatiles trigger male sexual arousal, initiating courtship sequences. Visual motion from group dynamics further amplifies arousal, creating a multisensory feedback loop that coordinates courtship across individuals. The findings suggest environmental cues act as critical gatekeepers for mating success in this species.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Food volatiles directly promote male sexual arousal in Drosophila erecta",
    "Visual motion from group dynamics amplifies male arousal through multisensory feedback",
    "Drosophila erecta requires environmental cues for courtship, unlike Drosophila melanogaster where food odors are dispensable"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study reveals how environmental cues can act as strict sensory gatekeepers for courtship behavior, highlighting a mechanism by which ecological context coordinates reproductive opportunities within social groups."
}
